# Relay third-party notices

This file describes the native `@RELAY_NOTICE_PLATFORM@` release payload. It is
generated at package time so its versions and source locations stay attached to
the artifact they describe.

## Relay

Relay's own source is distributed under the MIT License. The complete terms
are included beside this file as `Relay-MIT.txt`.

## Qt @RELAY_NOTICE_QT_VERSION@

Relay uses Qt dynamically under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 3. The complete license is included as `Qt-LGPL-3.0.txt`.

Corresponding source for the exact packaged Qt version:

@RELAY_QT_SOURCE_URI@

The Qt shared libraries remain replaceable. Relay does not prohibit reverse
engineering for debugging modifications to those libraries. Qt also contains
third-party components under their own licenses; the authoritative SPDX SBOM
and notices from the selected Qt distribution must be retained with the release
source record.

## Git @RELAY_NOTICE_GIT_VERSION@

Bundled in this artifact: `@RELAY_NOTICE_GIT_BUNDLED@`.

Git is a separate child-process program distributed under GPL-2.0-only. When
bundled, the complete license is included as `Git-GPL-2.0.txt` and component
licenses present in the runtime tree remain in that tree.

Corresponding source for the exact packaged Git distribution, including the
redistributed Git for Windows/MSYS2 components where applicable:

@RELAY_GIT_SOURCE_URI@

## GitHub CLI @RELAY_NOTICE_GH_VERSION@

Bundled in this artifact: `@RELAY_NOTICE_GIT_BUNDLED@`.

GitHub CLI is a separate child-process program distributed under the MIT
License. When bundled, the complete terms are included as
`GitHub-CLI-MIT.txt`.

Source for the exact packaged GitHub CLI version:

@RELAY_GH_SOURCE_URI@

These notices are a release-engineering record, not legal advice.
